 3. 🗳️ GOP struggles in key gov races 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 With midterms 57 days away, a warning light is blinking for Senate Republicans: underperforming gubernatorial nominees in three crucial Midwest states — Michigan, Iowa and Ohio.

 Why it matters: Strong candidates for governor can act as sheepdogs in tight Senate races, keeping Republican voters — and GOP-curious independents — moving in the party's direction, Axios' Hans Nichols reports. 👀 This is adding to GOP anxiety in Michigan and Iowa, where the Democratic gubernatorial nominees have led for much of the summer.

 In Ohio — a state President Trump won by 11 points — the governor's race is tied. The other side: The GOP is strong in several governor races.

 Republicans are enthusiastic about Georgia, where the gubernatorial race between former Atlanta Mayor Keisha Lance Bottoms (D) and health care executive Rick Jackson (R) is tight , but Jackson is expected to spend heavily in the final months. In Texas, Gov. Greg Abbott (R) leads state Rep. Gina Hinojosa (D) 47% to 44%, per 270toWin . In New Hampshire, Gov. Kelly Ayotte (R) leads former Executive Councilor Cinde Warmington (D) by an average of 49% to 39% . Read on . 

 
 
