 6. 🤖 AI&#x27;s classroom reckoning 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios. Stock: Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 America's two largest school districts both imposed sweeping AI bans this past week, hitting the brakes on a technology that's rapidly making its way into classrooms around the country.

 Why it matters: Some studies have found personalized AI tutors can improve learning. But other research has linked AI-assisted essay writing to weaker critical thinking, Axios' Josephine Walker reports. 🎒 New York City's public school district blocked AI use for roughly 600,000 students in pre-K through 8th grade and restricted it to specific uses in high school.

 Hours later, Los Angeles Unified imposed a districtwide moratorium on AI use on school devices for this school year. What we're watching: Chicago school board candidates have signed a pledge demanding a three-year moratorium on generative AI in the city's schools.

